  "limitations": [
    "The dissimilarities between our experimental situation and the urban environment limit the generality of our findings to macro crowding phenomena.",
    "subjects in our study, unlike the inhabitants of a crowded city, experience crowding for a relatively short period of time and realize that they will eventually leave the situation.",
    "Since this experiment did not control for or manipulate the factor of time, however, it is impossible to ascertain whether the perception of crowding actually decreased over time within the small room, competitive condition.",
    "it was impossible to ascertain, in this experiment, whether the increased level of laughter and noise perceived in the small room, competitive condition reflected the absence of crowding, a mode of coping with it, or even a nonspatial source of heightened crowding."
  ],
